# The baked shaders ARE tracked, all 16KB of them. They are build output, which normally has no
# place in a repository — but they are the difference between a clone that works and a clone that
# draws no background at all, and keeping them turns installing this into `git clone` and nothing
# else. Rebuild them with assets/build-shaders.sh after editing a .frag.

# Nothing the shell writes lands in the tree — settings go to $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/nothingshell,
# generated state to $XDG_STATE_HOME (see Paths.qml). These catch a leftover from the old layout.
settings.json
assets/theme.json

# Written by quickshell when it is run with this file present; it points QML tooling at the
# generated type information for the `qs.*` module imports. Machine-specific paths.
.qmlls.ini

# The theme videos — ~196MB — ARE tracked: a theme without its background is not the theme. That
# puts the repository around 200MB, and GitHub warns (but does not refuse) on the two files over
# 50MB. If that ever becomes a problem, git-lfs for *.mp4 is the answer, not deleting them.

# Machine-specific: which account the greeter logs in and what session it starts. Generated by
# greeter/install.sh from the user it was sudo'd from; greeter.json.example documents the shape.
greeter/greeter.json

.claude/
